---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About"
	description="Who we are and why we're building this"
	pubDate={new Date()}
>
	<h2>The Manifesto</h2>
	
	<p>
		We are the ones who couldn't sit still in school. Who got told we had "so much potential" 
		if we'd just <em>apply ourselves</em>. Who learned to mask, to perform normalcy, to pretend 
		our brains worked like everyone else's.
	</p>

	<p>
		We're done pretending.
	</p>

	<p>
		Our brains are not broken. They're running different firmware. The same minds that "can't focus" 
		can hyperfocus so intensely that time dissolves. The same minds that "can't follow instructions" 
		can see patterns and connections that others miss entirely.
	</p>

	<p>
		The problem isn't us. The problem is tools built for a brain type that isn't ours.
	</p>

	<h2>What We're Building</h2>

	<p>
		Cognitive Elitist exists to serve minds that work different. We build tools, share knowledge, 
		and create community for people whose brains don't fit the neurotypical mold.
	</p>

	<p>
		Everything we make is guided by a few principles:
	</p>

	<ul>
		<li><strong>Work with the brain, not against it.</strong> No more "just try harder." Systems that leverage how we actually think.</li>
		<li><strong>Privacy by default.</strong> Your thoughts, your data, your business. We don't sell you, we sell software.</li>
		<li><strong>One-time purchases over subscriptions.</strong> Stop renting your tools. Own them.</li>
		<li><strong>No apologies.</strong> We're not broken. We're not less than. We're different, and that's our edge.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Who's Behind This</h2>

	<p>
		This project is built by <a href="https://cheatcoders.ai">CheatCoders</a>—a small team 
		that understands the struggle because we live it. We're not productivity consultants 
		who read a book about ADHD. We're neurodivergent builders making tools we wish existed.
	</p>

	<h2>Join Us</h2>

	<p>
		If your brain works different, you're welcome here. Follow us on 
		<a href="https://twitter.com/cognitiveelite">Twitter</a> for updates, hot takes, 
		and tools that actually work.
	</p>

	<p>
		<em>The elite aren't born. They're just different. And they stopped apologizing for it.</em>
	</p>
</Layout>

<style>
	h2 {
		margin-top: 2.5em;
		color: var(--text-primary);
	}
	h2:first-of-type {
		margin-top: 0;
	}
	ul {
		list-style: none;
		padding: 0;
	}
	ul li {
		padding: 0.75em 0;
		padding-left: 1.5em;
		position: relative;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
	}
	ul li:last-child {
		border-bottom: none;
	}
	ul li::before {
		content: "◆";
		position: absolute;
		left: 0;
		color: var(--accent);
		font-size: 0.6em;
		top: 1.1em;
	}
</style>
